module

public import StacksFrontier.Algebra.Category.ModuleCat.Sheaf.PushforwardFullyFaithful.Basic
public import StacksFrontier.Algebra.Category.ModuleCat.Sheaf.ToposModuleRestriction
public import StacksFrontier.CategoryTheory.Sites.MorphismOfSites.TopologicalComparison
public import StacksFrontier.Topology.Sheaves.Functors.Module.RingedSpace
public import StacksFrontier.Algebra.Category.ModuleCat.Sheaf.PushforwardEssentialImage
public import StacksFrontier.Topology.Sheaves.ClosedImmersion.Pushforward
public import Mathlib.AlgebraicGeometry.Modules.Sheaf

/-!
# A ringed space as a ringed topos

A ringed space `(X, 𝒪_X)` presents a ringed topos: the site is the lattice of opens of `X` with
the topology generated by open coverings, and the structure sheaf is `𝒪_X`. A morphism of ringed
spaces presents a morphism of ringed topoi, the underlying morphism of topoi being the one
attached by Stacks 00X2 to the continuous functor `V ↦ f⁻¹ V` and the structure map being `f^♯`.

This file builds that presentation and identifies the direct image of sheaves of modules it
induces with the ordinary one. The identification is the point: the ringed-topos development
transports the module structure on `f_* M` through the sections functor, whereas
`CategoryTheory.SheafOfModules.pushforward` restricts scalars along `f^♯` sectionwise, so the
two are *different* sheaves of modules over different (isomorphic) sheaves of rings and a
comparison is needed. The comparison is the identity on sections; its content is
`Stacks.Sheaves.ToposPullback.restrictionModuleIso`.

By contrast, the two *scheme-level* spellings of the direct image in this repository —
`AlgebraicGeometry.Scheme.Modules.pushforward` and
`RingedSpaceModuleAdjunction.modulePushforward` applied to the underlying morphism of ringed
spaces — are definitionally equal, which is recorded here as
`Stacks.ToposBridge.scheme_modules_pushforward_eq`.

## Main definitions

* `Stacks.ToposBridge.ringedTopos`: the ringed topos presented by a ringed space.
* `Stacks.ToposBridge.morphismOfTopoi`: the morphism of topoi presented by a morphism of ringed
  spaces.
* `Stacks.ToposBridge.ringedToposHom`: the morphism of ringed topoi presented by a morphism of
  ringed spaces.
* `Stacks.ToposBridge.pushforwardModulesIso`: the comparison of the two direct images on sheaves
  of modules.

## Main results

* `Stacks.ToposBridge.scheme_modules_pushforward_eq`: for a morphism of schemes, the
  scheme-level direct image of sheaves of modules *is* the ringed-space-level one.
* `Stacks.ToposBridge.scheme_modules_pullback_eq`: the same for the pullback.  For the
  adjunction between the two it is
  `Stacks.ModuleSkyscraper.pullbackPushforwardAdjunction_eq_modulePullbackPushforwardAdjunction`.
* `Stacks.ToposBridge.schemePushforwardModulesIso`: consequently the ringed-topos direct image
  is isomorphic to `AlgebraicGeometry.Scheme.Modules.pushforward`.

## Implementation notes

The structure map of a `AlgebraicGeometry.RingedToposHom` is a morphism into
`Stacks.Sheaves.ToposPushforward.pushforwardCommRingFunctor`, the direct image of a sheaf of
commutative rings along a morphism of *topoi*, whereas `f^♯` is a morphism into the direct image
along the *continuous functor* `V ↦ f⁻¹ V`. Those two sheaves of commutative rings have the same
underlying sheaf of sets and different (equal) ring structures, and
`Stacks.Sheaves.ToposPullback.restrictionCommRingIso` identifies them; it is the identity on
underlying sheaves of sets, which is what makes `structureRingMap_eq` below hold and what will
carry a surjectivity hypothesis across.

## References

* [Stacks Project, Tag 01D3](https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/01D3)
* [Stacks Project, Tag 00X2](https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/00X2)
* [Stacks Project, Tag 03D6](https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/03D6)
-/

@[expose] public noncomputable section

open CategoryTheory CategoryTheory.Limits TopologicalSpace AlgebraicGeometry
open Stacks.Sheaves.ToposPushforward Stacks.Sheaves.ToposPullback

universe u

namespace Stacks.ToposBridge

/-- The ringed topos presented by a ringed space: the small Zariski site of its underlying
topological space, together with its structure sheaf. -/
def ringedTopos (X : RingedSpace.{u, u}) : RingedTopos.{u, u, u} where
  C := Opens X.carrier
  J := Opens.grothendieckTopology X.carrier
  O := X.sheaf

variable {X Y : RingedSpace.{u, u}} (f : X ⟶ Y)

/-- **Stacks 00X2.** The morphism of topoi presented by a morphism of ringed spaces: the one
attached to the continuous functor `V ↦ f⁻¹ V` between the small Zariski sites. -/
def morphismOfTopoi : MorphismOfTopoi (ringedTopos X).Topos (ringedTopos Y).Topos :=
  (StacksZariskiSite.isMorphismOfSites_opensMap f.hom.base).morphismOfTopoi

/-- The direct image of the morphism of topoi presented by `f` is the direct image of sheaves of
sets along the continuous functor `V ↦ f⁻¹ V`. -/
theorem morphismOfTopoi_pushforward :
    (morphismOfTopoi f).pushforward =
      (Opens.map f.hom.base).sheafPushforwardContinuous (Type u)
        (Opens.grothendieckTopology Y.carrier) (Opens.grothendieckTopology X.carrier) :=
  rfl

/-- The component `f^♯ : 𝒪_Y ⟶ f_* 𝒪_X` of a morphism of ringed spaces, read as a morphism of
sheaves of commutative rings on the small Zariski site of `Y` whose target is the direct image
along the continuous functor `V ↦ f⁻¹ V`. -/
def commRingStructureHom :
    Y.sheaf ⟶ ((Opens.map f.hom.base).sheafPushforwardContinuous CommRingCat.{u}
      (Opens.grothendieckTopology Y.carrier)
      (Opens.grothendieckTopology X.carrier)).obj X.sheaf :=
  ⟨f.hom.c⟩

/-- **Stacks 01D3, part (2).** The morphism of ringed topoi presented by a morphism of ringed
spaces. Its structure map is `f^♯`, read into the topos-level direct image of the structure sheaf
through `Stacks.Sheaves.ToposPullback.restrictionCommRingIso`. -/
def ringedToposHom : RingedToposHom (ringedTopos X) (ringedTopos Y) where
  toToposHom := morphismOfTopoi f
  fSharp := commRingStructureHom f ≫
    (restrictionCommRingIso (Opens.grothendieckTopology Y.carrier)
      (Opens.grothendieckTopology X.carrier) (Opens.map f.hom.base) X.sheaf).inv

/-- The underlying morphism of topoi of `Stacks.ToposBridge.ringedToposHom`. -/
@[simp]
theorem ringedToposHom_toToposHom :
    (ringedToposHom f).toToposHom = morphismOfTopoi f :=
  rfl

/-- The structure map of `Stacks.ToposBridge.ringedToposHom`, at the level of sheaves of rings,
is `f^♯` followed by the comparison of the topos-level direct image with restriction along the
continuous functor. In particular it is `f^♯` on underlying sheaves of sets, the comparison being
the identity there. -/
theorem structureRingMap_eq :
    (ringedToposHom f).structureRingMap =
      RingedSpaceModuleAdjunction.structureSheafHom f ≫
        (restrictionRingIso (Opens.grothendieckTopology Y.carrier)
          (Opens.grothendieckTopology X.carrier) (Opens.map f.hom.base)
          (structureSheafRing X)).inv :=
  rfl

/-- The comparison of the structure map with `f^♯` is undone by composing with the comparison of
the two direct images of the structure sheaf of rings. -/
theorem structureRingMap_comp_restrictionRingIso_hom :
    (ringedToposHom f).structureRingMap ≫
        (restrictionRingIso (Opens.grothendieckTopology Y.carrier)
          (Opens.grothendieckTopology X.carrier) (Opens.map f.hom.base)
          (structureSheafRing X)).hom =
      RingedSpaceModuleAdjunction.structureSheafHom f :=
  rfl


/-! ### The comparison of the two direct images on sheaves of modules -/

/-- The structure map of a morphism of ringed spaces, read at the level of sheaves of rings and
into the topos-level direct image of the structure sheaf of rings. This is the datum that
`Stacks.Sheaves.PushforwardEssentialImage.pushforwardModules` consumes, and it is `f^♯` on
underlying sheaves of sets. -/
def toposStructureRingMap :
    structureSheafRing Y ⟶
      pushforwardRingSheaf.{u, u, u, u, u, u} (morphismOfTopoi f)
        (structureSheafRing X) :=
  RingedSpaceModuleAdjunction.structureSheafHom f ≫
    (restrictionRingIso (Opens.grothendieckTopology Y.carrier)
      (Opens.grothendieckTopology X.carrier) (Opens.map f.hom.base)
      (structureSheafRing X)).inv

/-- The structure map of `Stacks.ToposBridge.ringedToposHom`, read at the level of sheaves of
rings, is `Stacks.ToposBridge.toposStructureRingMap`. -/
theorem structureRingMap_eq_toposStructureRingMap :
    (ringedToposHom f).structureRingMap = toposStructureRingMap f :=
  rfl

/-- **Stacks 03D6, part (1), for a morphism of ringed spaces.** The direct image of sheaves of
modules determined by the morphism of topoi presented by `f` and by the structure map of `f` is
the ordinary direct image of sheaves of modules along `f`.

The two functors are not equal. The topos-level one carries the module structure transported
along the sections functor, over the topos-level direct image
`Stacks.Sheaves.ToposPushforward.pushforwardRingSheaf` of the structure sheaf of rings, and the
ordinary one restricts scalars along `f^♯` sectionwise over the restriction of the structure sheaf
of rings along the continuous functor `V ↦ f⁻¹ V`. The comparison is the identity on sections: it
is `Stacks.Sheaves.ToposPullback.restrictionModuleIso` whiskered with restriction of scalars along
the structure map, after which the two remaining restrictions of scalars compose to restriction
along `f^♯`, by `Stacks.ToposBridge.structureRingMap_comp_restrictionRingIso_hom`. -/
def pushforwardModulesIso :
    Stacks.Sheaves.PushforwardEssentialImage.pushforwardModules.{u, u, u, u, u}
        (morphismOfTopoi f) (structureSheafRing X)
        (toposStructureRingMap f) ≅
      RingedSpaceModuleAdjunction.modulePushforward f :=
  by
  refine Iso.trans (Functor.isoWhiskerRight
    (restrictionModuleIso (Opens.grothendieckTopology Y.carrier)
      (Opens.grothendieckTopology X.carrier) (Opens.map f.hom.base)
      (structureSheafRing X))
    (SheafOfModules.restrictScalars (toposStructureRingMap f))) (eqToIso ?_)
  rfl

/-! ### Embeddings -/

/-- For a morphism of ringed spaces whose underlying continuous map is inducing — in particular
for a closed immersion — the direct image on sheaves of sets of the presented morphism of topoi
is fully faithful.

This is `ClosedImmersionSheaves.sheafPushforwardFullyFaithful`, whose conclusion is about
`TopCat.Sheaf.pushforward`; that functor *is* the direct image along the continuous functor
`V ↦ f⁻¹ V` (Stacks 00X2), hence is the direct image of the presented morphism of topoi. -/
def fullyFaithfulPushforward (hf : Topology.IsInducing f.hom.base) :
    (morphismOfTopoi f).pushforward.FullyFaithful :=
  ClosedImmersionSheaves.sheafPushforwardFullyFaithful (C := Type u) hf

/-- **Stacks 08LU for a morphism of ringed spaces with inducing underlying map.** The presented
morphism of topoi is an embedding. -/
theorem isEmbedding_morphismOfTopoi (hf : Topology.IsInducing f.hom.base) :
    (morphismOfTopoi f).IsEmbedding :=
  ⟨(fullyFaithfulPushforward f hf).full, (fullyFaithfulPushforward f hf).faithful⟩

/-! ### Schemes -/

/-- **The two scheme-level spellings of the direct image of sheaves of modules agree on the
nose.** For a morphism of schemes `f`, the scheme-level direct image
`AlgebraicGeometry.Scheme.Modules.pushforward f` and the ringed-space-level direct image
`RingedSpaceModuleAdjunction.modulePushforward` of the underlying morphism of ringed spaces are
definitionally equal: `AlgebraicGeometry.Scheme.ringCatSheaf` and
`structureSheafRing` are the same composition with `forget₂ CommRingCat
RingCat`, and `AlgebraicGeometry.Scheme.Hom.toRingCatSheafHom` and
`RingedSpaceModuleAdjunction.structureSheafHom` are the same whiskering of `f^♯`. -/
theorem scheme_modules_pushforward_eq {X Y : Scheme.{u}} (f : X ⟶ Y) :
    Scheme.Modules.pushforward f =
      RingedSpaceModuleAdjunction.modulePushforward f.toLRSHom.toShHom :=
  rfl

/-- The two scheme-level spellings of the *pullback* of sheaves of modules also agree on the
nose: `CategoryTheory.SheafOfModules.pullback` is a chosen left adjoint, and
`CategoryTheory.Functor.IsRightAdjoint` is a `Prop`, so the two spellings of the right
adjointness witness do not separate the two chosen left adjoints. -/
theorem scheme_modules_pullback_eq {X Y : Scheme.{u}} (f : X ⟶ Y) :
    Scheme.Modules.pullback f =
      RingedSpaceModuleAdjunction.modulePullback f.toLRSHom.toShHom :=
  rfl

/-- The scheme-level form of `Stacks.ToposBridge.pushforwardModulesIso`: the direct image of
sheaves of modules determined by the morphism of topoi presented by a morphism of schemes is
`AlgebraicGeometry.Scheme.Modules.pushforward`. -/
def schemePushforwardModulesIso {X Y : Scheme.{u}} (f : X ⟶ Y) :
    Stacks.Sheaves.PushforwardEssentialImage.pushforwardModules.{u, u, u, u, u}
        (morphismOfTopoi f.toLRSHom.toShHom)
        (structureSheafRing X.toRingedSpace)
        (toposStructureRingMap f.toLRSHom.toShHom) ≅
      Scheme.Modules.pushforward f :=
  pushforwardModulesIso f.toLRSHom.toShHom

end Stacks.ToposBridge

end
